    {
      "id": "c4f96db5-ec88-5a6e-b13d-aa56a8e07e9d",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -620,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 500,
        "height": 860,
        "content": "## Follow up on unanswered quotes, and stop the moment the customer replies\n\nMany quotes are lost simply because nobody followed up, and a follow-up after the customer already answered looks careless. This workflow chases every quote still waiting and checks your Gmail inbox first.\n\n### How it works\n1. Every weekday at 9am, except the public holidays you list, it reads the **Requests** tab and keeps the quotes with Status *Quote sent*.\n2. It searches Gmail for messages from those customers received after the quote was sent.\n3. A customer who replied leaves the sequence: Status *Replied* (*Unsubscribed* if they wrote STOP) and **Replied At** are written to the sheet.\n4. The others get the next email (default: 2, 5, 10 and 20 days after the quote, counted in calendar days): questions, quick call, scheduling, then a polite \"should I close your file?\".\n5. You receive one summary: who replied (call them back), who was chased, how many are due on the next run.\n\n### Setup\n- Connect **Gmail** and **Google Sheets** credentials.\n- Fill the **Config** node: Sheet ID, company, your name, email and phone, currency, holidays.\n- Set the time zone in the workflow settings.\n- Uses one Google Sheet with three tabs \u2014 **Requests**, **Appointments**, **Equipment** \u2014 shared by the whole Home Services Automation Kit (column list in the README).\n- When you send a quote: set Status = *Quote sent*, the amount and **Quote Sent At**.\n\n### Customization tips\n- Change `followUpDays` to lengthen or shorten the sequence.\n- Edit the texts and STOP words in **Plan today's quote follow-ups**."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
